{
  "response": "**VERDICT: REJECT**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The `BuggyFileInput` component exhibits critical accessibility failures in semantic structure, accessible naming, error association, and state communication. While the input renders native file controls and an `accept` attribute, it lacks an programmatic label (`<label>` or `aria-labelledby`), fails to expose error state (`aria-invalid`), silences validation errors for screen reader users (no `aria-describedby` or live announcement), and conceals size constraints until after failure.\n\n---\n\n### Pre-commitment Predictions\nBefore reviewing the code, common file input design anti-patterns were predicted:\n1. Visual label rendered in an unassociated `<div>` rather than a native `<label htmlFor=\"...\">`. *(Confirmed: line 19)*\n2. Error message rendered visually without programmatic linkage via `aria-describedby` or live region. *(Confirmed: lines 25\u201329)*\n3. Input missing `aria-invalid=\"true\"` when an error is active. *(Confirmed: lines 20\u201324)*\n4. File requirements (size limit and accepted formats) not presented as accessible helper text. *(Confirmed: lines 19\u201324)*\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings (Blocks Access)\n\n1. **Unassociated visual text container used in place of native `<label>`**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-24`\n   - **Element**: `<div>Upload file</div>` preceding `<input type=\"file\" />`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users, speech-input users, low vision and motor-impaired users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships - Level A), SC 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions - Level A), SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: A plain `<div>` has no semantic role. The file input has no accessible name. Assistive technologies will announce only the user-agent fallback (e.g., \"Choose File, button\" or \"Upload, button\") with zero context regarding what file is requested. Furthermore, clicking the text will not activate or focus the file picker.\n   - **Fix**: Replace `<div>Upload file</div>` with `<label htmlFor=\"file-upload-input\">Upload file</label>` and add `id=\"file-upload-input\"` to the `<input>`.\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: file-input-missing-label\nfingerprint: c3a48e71b2d91f04\nsource: BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-24\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships, SC 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions, SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value\nsection_508_fpc_context: WCAG 2.0 SC 1.3.1, 3.3.2, 4.1.2 (508 Chapter 5 - 501.1)\nseverity: CRITICAL\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard=LOW, low_vision=MEDIUM, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: <div>Upload file</div><input type=\"file\" onChange={handleFileChange} accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\" />\nreproduction_steps: Inspect accessibility tree for <input type=\"file\" />.\nexpected_behavior: Accessible name is computed from the visible label (\"Upload file\").\nactual_behavior: Accessible name is empty or falls back to browser-default \"Choose File\".\ntrend: new\n```\n\n2. **Validation error is neither associated with the input nor announced to assistive technology**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:25-29`\n   - **Element**: `{error && <div className=\"error-message\">{error}</div>}`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users, blind and low vision users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships - Level A), SC 3.3.1 (Error Identification - Level A), SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages - Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When an oversized file is selected, the file input rejects it and sets an error string. However, the error container is neither linked via `aria-describedby` nor announced via an accessible status/live mechanism. Because focus remains inside the file input or returns to the page with no notification, a screen reader user is completely unaware that upload failed.\n   - **Fix**: Assign an `id` (e.g., `id=\"file-error\"`) to the error container, bind it to the `<input>` via `aria-describedby=\"file-error\"`, and supply dynamic status feedback (or ensure the persistent description container is referenced).\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings (Significantly Degrades Experience)\n\n1. **Input does not communicate invalid state (`aria-invalid`)**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:20-24`\n   - **Element**: `<input type=\"file\" ... />`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users, braille display users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A), SC 3.3.1 (Error Identification - Level A).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When validation fails, the control does not reflect its error state programmatically. Screen readers will not announce that the field is invalid when re-focused or inspected.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-invalid={error ? 'true' : 'false'}` to the `<input>`.\n\n2. **Error message lacks actionable correction instructions**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:9`\n   - **Element**: `setError('File too large');`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Cognitive accessibility users, all users encountering the error.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.3 (Error Suggestion - Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: \"File too large\" does not specify the maximum allowable file size (5MB). Users are forced to guess acceptable thresholds through trial and error.\n   - **Fix**: Change error text to be explicit and actionable: `\"File exceeds the 5MB size limit. Please choose a smaller file.\"`\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings (Friction but Workaround Exists)\n\n1. **File constraints communicated only through HTML file picker filter, not in text instructions**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:23`\n   - **Element**: `accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\"`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Cognitive users, low vision users, screen reader users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions - Level A).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: While `accept` restricts the OS file picker dialog, users are not provided upfront text explaining allowed formats (`.pdf`, `.doc`, `.docx`) or file size limitations (< 5MB) before opening the dialog.\n   - **Fix**: Add an instructional helper text element (e.g., `<p id=\"file-instructions\">Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX (Max 5MB)</p>`) and reference it in the input's `aria-describedby`.\n\n---\n\n### Enhancements (Best Practice)\n\n1. **Clear visual and programmatic indicator when a valid file is chosen**: Provide explicit text feedback showing the currently selected file name and size, allowing users to verify their selection before submission.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing (Gaps & Unhandled Edge Cases)\n\n- **Missing programmatic association**: No `id`/`htmlFor` relationship between label and `<input>`.\n- **Missing composite `aria-describedby` linking**: Neither instructions nor the dynamic error are referenced by the input's description list (`aria-describedby={error ? 'file-instructions file-error' : 'file-instructions'}`).\n- **Missing upfront size constraints**: The 5MB constraint is hardcoded into `handleFileChange` (`file.size > 5000000`) without any visual or programmatic guidance prior to user failure.\n\n---\n\n### Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Input lacks accessible name; error is not announced or associated; invalid state omitted. |\n| Keyboard-only | **LOW** | Native `<input type=\"file\" />` is keyboard operable via Tab and Space/Enter. |\n| Low vision | **MEDIUM** | Label text is non-clickable (reduces hit target area); error visibility and contrast need confirmation. |\n| Cognitive | **MEDIUM** | Ambiguous error (\"File too large\"); missing upfront size and type instructions. |\n| Vestibular & motion | **LOW** | No animation or motion triggers present. |\n| Auditory access | **LOW** | No audio elements or auditory notifications. |\n| Environmental contrast | **MEDIUM** | CSS classes (`.error-message`, `.file-upload`) must be verified for 4.5:1 text contrast. |\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen Reader User**: Navigating to this field presents an unlabelled file upload control. If an invalid file is selected, the file picker closes, focus returns to the input, and the screen reader remains silent\u2014leaving the user to assume the file was accepted.\n- **Keyboard-only User**: Can activate the dialog with Space/Enter. However, clicking the label text fails to trigger the input because it is an unlinked `<div>`.\n- **Low Vision User**: Clicking the visible label does not focus the input. If `.error-message` relies solely on color (e.g., red text with no accompanying icon or border), it risks failing WCAG 1.4.1.\n- **Cognitive Accessibility**: Error feedback provides no remediation guidance (fails to mention the 5MB ceiling), inducing repetitive failed attempts.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Remediation\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState } from 'react';\n\nconst AccessibleFileInput = () => {\n  const [selectedFile, setSelectedFile] = useState(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n\n  const MAX_SIZE_BYTES = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5MB\n\n  const handleFileChange = (e) => {\n    const file = e.target.files[0];\n    if (file && file.size > MAX_SIZE_BYTES) {\n      setError('File exceeds the 5MB limit. Please upload a file under 5MB.');\n      setSelectedFile(null);\n    } else {\n      setSelectedFile(file || null);\n      setError(null);\n    }\n  };\n\n  const errorId = 'file-upload-error';\n  const instructionsId = 'file-upload-instructions';\n  const describedBy = error ? `${instructionsId} ${errorId}` : instructionsId;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-upload\">\n      <label htmlFor=\"file-upload-input\" className=\"file-upload-label\">\n        Upload file\n      </label>\n\n      <p id={instructionsId} className=\"file-upload-instructions\">\n        Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX (Maximum size: 5MB)\n      </p>\n\n      <input\n        id=\"file-upload-input\"\n        type=\"file\"\n        onChange={handleFileChange}\n        accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\"\n        aria-describedby={describedBy}\n        aria-invalid={error ? 'true' : 'false'}\n      />\n\n      {error && (\n        <div id={errorId} className=\"error-message\" role=\"alert\">\n          {error}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {selectedFile && !error && (\n        <p className=\"file-upload-success\" role=\"status\">\n          Selected file: {selectedFile.name}\n        </p>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default AccessibleFileInput;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n\n**REJECT**: The component fails multiple Level A criteria (WCAG 1.3.1, 3.3.1, 3.3.2, 4.1.2). Assistive technology users cannot perceive the input's purpose, are not informed of input constraints, and receive zero feedback upon validation failure. Remediation requires replacing the `<div>` label with a semantic `<label htmlFor=\"...\">`, linking instructions and dynamic errors via `aria-describedby`, communicating error state with `aria-invalid`, and revising the error copy per WCAG 3.3.3.\n\n### Open Questions (Unscored)\n- Is the error container intended to announce automatically via `role=\"alert\"` or polite status region, or is the form validated on submit?\n- Are CSS contrast levels verified for `.error-message` against its container background (\u2265 4.5:1)?\n",
